; The installer's texts. The first block replaces Tauri's own English strings; the "qm" ones
; belong to the parts marked "QM:" in installer.nsi.
LangString addOrReinstall ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Install it again"
LangString alreadyInstalled ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Already installed"
LangString alreadyInstalledLong ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} ${VERSION} is already installed. Choose what to do and click Next."
LangString appRunning ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} is running. Close it, then try again."
LangString appRunningOkKill ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} is running.$\nClick OK to close it."
LangString chooseMaintenanceOption ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Choose what to do with this install."
LangString chooseHowToInstall ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Choose how to install ${PRODUCTNAME}."
LangString createDesktop ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Put a shortcut on the desktop"
LangString dontUninstall ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Install over it"
LangString dontUninstallDowngrade ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Install over it (this installer cannot go back to an older version that way)"
LangString failedToKillApp ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} could not be closed. Close it, then try again."
LangString installingWebview2 ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Installing WebView2, which the launcher's window needs..."
LangString newerVersionInstalled ${LANG_ENGLISH} "A newer ${PRODUCTNAME} is already installed. Going back to an older one is not recommended; if you want to, uninstall the newer one first. Your mods, profiles and saves are kept either way. Choose what to do and click Next."
LangString older ${LANG_ENGLISH} "older"
LangString olderOrUnknownVersionInstalled ${LANG_ENGLISH} "An $R4 ${PRODUCTNAME} is installed. Setup can remove it first or install over it. Your mods, profiles and saves are kept either way. Choose what to do and click Next."
LangString silentDowngrades ${LANG_ENGLISH} "This installer cannot go back to an older version silently. Run it normally instead.$\n"
LangString unableToUninstall ${LANG_ENGLISH} "The installed version could not be removed."
LangString uninstallApp ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Uninstall ${PRODUCTNAME}"
LangString uninstallBeforeInstalling ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Remove it first, then install"
LangString unknown ${LANG_ENGLISH} "unknown"
LangString webview2AbortError ${LANG_ENGLISH} "WebView2 could not be installed, and the launcher's window needs it. Run the installer again."
LangString webview2DownloadError ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Error: WebView2 could not be downloaded - $0"
LangString webview2DownloadSuccess ${LANG_ENGLISH} "WebView2 downloaded"
LangString webview2Downloading ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Downloading WebView2..."
LangString webview2InstallError ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Error: installing WebView2 failed with exit code $1"
LangString webview2InstallSuccess ${LANG_ENGLISH} "WebView2 installed"
LangString deleteAppData ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Also delete my mods, profiles, save slots, backups and settings"

LangString qmWelcomeTitle ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Welcome to ${PRODUCTNAME}"
LangString qmWelcomeText ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} installs, orders and updates mods for Mud and Blood, and starts the game with them.$\r$\n$\r$\nSetup puts ${PRODUCTNAME} ${VERSION} in a folder of its own. Your mods, profiles and save slots are kept there too. The game's own files are never changed.$\r$\n$\r$\nClose ${PRODUCTNAME} and Mud and Blood before you go on.$\r$\n$\r$\nClick Next to continue."
LangString qmOptionsTitle ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Command-line tool"
LangString qmOptionsSubtitle ${LANG_ENGLISH} "For people who make mods. Players can leave both on or turn both off."
LangString qmOptionsIntro ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} comes with qm, a small command-line tool that checks a mod for mistakes, packs it for release and shows what its patches change."
LangString qmInstallCli ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Install the qm command-line tool"
LangString qmInstallCliHelp ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Puts qm.exe beside the launcher."
LangString qmAddPath ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Add it to PATH"
LangString qmAddPathHelp ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Adds ${PRODUCTNAME}'s folder to this computer's PATH, so typing qm works in any terminal. Open a new terminal after Setup for it to take effect."
LangString qmFinishTitle ${LANG_ENGLISH} "${PRODUCTNAME} is ready"
LangString qmFinishText ${LANG_ENGLISH} "On its first start ${PRODUCTNAME} looks for Mud and Blood and your saves, and asks where you keep mods you are making.$\r$\n$\r$\nIf you installed QuarterMaster by hand before, it finds that too and offers to import your mods."
LangString qmRunNow ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Start ${PRODUCTNAME} now"
LangString qmStartMenu ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Add ${PRODUCTNAME} to the Start menu"
LangString qmWorkspaceKept ${LANG_ENGLISH} "Your mod workspace folder is never deleted, ticked or not. The game goes back to running without mods."
